### Payout runner suite in CI — gap CLOSED

- The gap left open by PR #82 — `.github/workflows/ci.yml` did **not** run
  `node --test .github/scripts/payouts-release-job.test.mjs`, so the suite
  guarding the fail-closed gate was executed only by hand — is **CLOSED**. The
  suite now runs in CI on every pull request and on every push to `main`.
- Added one repository-level job `payout-runner` / "Payout runner - tests" in
  `.github/workflows/ci.yml`: `ubuntu-latest`, `actions/checkout@v4`,
  `actions/setup-node@v4` with `node-version: "22"`, then the single step
  `node --test .github/scripts/payouts-release-job.test.mjs` run from the
  repository root. No dependency install: the suite uses only Node built-ins.
  The job carries no `if:`, so it runs on both `pull_request` and `push` to
  `main` through the existing triggers.
- The suite was not inserted into the `frontend`, `frontend-next` or `backend`
  jobs, and neither those jobs nor the payout runner logic were touched.
  `payouts-auto-release.yml` was not modified.
- The job uses no secret and no Actions variable, invokes no Edge Function and
  emits no payout. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` contains zero `secrets.`
  references and zero `service_role` occurrences.
- Hooking the suite to CI exposed a real defect the manual runs had hidden: on
  **Node 22** the test `fallisce al timeout` hung and the run ended 6 passed /
  9 cancelled. `AbortSignal.timeout()` in `payouts-release-job.mjs` uses an
  unref'd timer, and in that test the stub `fetchImpl` promise was the only
  pending work, so the event loop drained before the abort. Node 24, used
  locally, happened to survive it. Fixed **in the test only**, with a ref'd
  keep-alive timer cleared on abort: the runner logic was not touched, and if
  the abort ever stopped arriving the promise now rejects with a different
  message and the assertion fails instead of hanging.
- Files modified besides this one: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and
  `.github/scripts/payouts-release-job.test.mjs`.
- Shipped as PR #84, squash-merged to `bdfd2c7`. All four CI jobs passed on the
  final head `7a97286`, and `Payout runner - tests` reported **15 tests / 15
  pass / 0 fail / 0 cancelled** on `node-version: 22`, read from the job log and
  not merely from the green check. Netlify and Supabase Preview stayed skipped:
  the PR touches no migration and no application source.
- Verified after the merge, on the `push` run of `main` at `bdfd2c7` and not
  only on the pull request: all four jobs green, and `Payout runner - tests`
  again **15 / 15 pass / 0 fail / 0 cancelled** on Node 22. The job therefore
  really executes on both triggers.
- Local verification: `node --test .github/scripts/payouts-release-job.test.mjs`
  gives **15 passed / 0 failed**; `git diff --check` is clean; `ci.yml` was
  parsed with the `js-yaml` already present in `frontend/node_modules`, without
  installing anything, confirming the four jobs `frontend`, `frontend-next`,
